WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.576
Idea. A bacterium is a single cell. It is much smaller than a human cell. On the outside is a cell wall, which supports and protects the cell. Just inside it is the cell membrane, which controls what goes in and out. The cytoplasm fills the cell.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:36.795
A bacterium has no nucleus. Its DNA is one loop, free in the cytoplasm. Many bacteria also have plasmids: small extra rings of DNA. Ribosomes make proteins. A flagellum spins to move the cell. Some have a slime capsule outside the wall.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:54.297
Method. Now compare a human cell, like a skin cell. It has a cell membrane, cytoplasm and ribosomes. Its DNA is inside a nucleus. It has mitochondria, where respiration releases energy. It has no cell wall.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:01:07.115
Similarities first. Both cells have a cell membrane, cytoplasm and ribosomes. Both have DNA. In a bacterium it is a loose loop; in a human cell it is in a nucleus.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:23.687
Now differences. A bacterium has a cell wall; a human cell does not. A human cell has a nucleus; a bacterium does not. Bacteria often have plasmids. Human cells have mitochondria. Always say which cell has the structure.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:38.658
Learn one job for each part. The cell wall supports and protects. The membrane controls what enters and leaves. Ribosomes make proteins. DNA holds the genetic code. The flagellum moves the cell.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:50.925
Worked example. Here is a real exam question. The diagrams show a bacterial cell and a human skin cell. Give two differences between them. Two marks.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:02:02.697
Look at the bacterium: a thick outer wall and a long flagellum. The skin cell has no wall. Difference one: the bacterial cell has a cell wall, but the skin cell does not.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:16.048
The skin cell has a clear nucleus. The bacterium has none; its DNA is free in the cytoplasm. That is difference two. Answer by olevels.com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:22.349
So the full answer is two sentences. Each one names a structure and says which cell has it.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:34.211
Common mistake. A common mistake is to say a bacterium has no DNA, because it has no nucleus. It does have DNA, as one loop in the cytoplasm.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:43.897
Another mistake is a difference with no direction, like just 'cell wall'. Or saying only one cell has a membrane. Both cells have a membrane.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:03:00.162
Your turn. A sperm cell is a human cell. Compare it with a bacterium. Give two structures found in both cells, and one structure found only in the bacterium. Then state the job of ribosomes. Pause here and work it out.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:12.421
Answer. Both cells have a cell membrane, cytoplasm and ribosomes. The bacterial ribosomes are smaller. Both also have DNA. Give any two of these.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:18.939
Only the bacterium has a cell wall. Plasmids also count. Ribosomes make proteins.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:29.413
So, every time: read whether the question wants similarities or differences. For a difference, name the structure and say which cell has it.
